    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of parked vehicles and obstructions could significantly improve apparatus ingress and egress during an emergency response. Displaying a clearly visible address marker at the street frontage would assist responding units in locating the property quickly. Maintaining adequate turnaround space near the main building and detached structure would support apparatus positioning and staging. Trimming or managing dense vegetation along the driveway and access road could improve driver visibility and reduce travel time for responding units. Identifying and communicating any secondary access opportunities around the rear of the property to the local fire department in advance may assist with pre-incident planning."
