    "recommendations": "Reducing brush directly adjacent to the structure and creating greater separation between dense shrub cover and building surfaces could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce opportunities for fire to reach the structure. Managing ladder fuels beneath and around tree clusters would help interrupt vertical fuel continuity, reducing the potential for fire to move from ground-level vegetation into the tree canopy. Thinning and separating scattered shrubs and heavy brush within the immediate structure perimeter may further reduce fuel continuity across the property. Where mixed vegetation cover surrounds the structure on multiple sides, maintaining cleared or well-separated zones could improve conditions for suppression operations. Given the single access route serving the property, keeping that route clear of overhanging vegetation and encroaching brush on both sides would support firefighter access and improve evacuation movement. Continued attention to vegetation management within the structure's immediate surroundings would support long-term wildfire resilience at this wildland interface location."
